From 346c4cb64d235254a9163491a0d09ba3904e9425 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:19:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban parent_missing self-clear: parents_unlinked
 timeline source; repair note is a system comment

Follow-up to PR #2192 review (GitHub review 5891026555, card t_01a1d4df1d71df8b).

1. Parentless timeline. When every parent link is removed while the
   detector's block holds, note_missing_parents returns early on empty
   states, so no parent_found is ever written. The unblocked payload and
   the repair-card note still said "cleared via parent_found". The unblock
   now records source=parents_unlinked in that case (parent_found only
   when parents exist and are all present again); `parents` keeps naming
   the ids the block was about.
2. Repair-comment provenance. add_comment stamps writer_run_id/uid from
   HERMES_KANBAN_TASK/RUN_ID. When recompute_ready runs inside the repair
   card's own worker, the note was recorded as that run's own comment and
   the live comment bridge skipped it for exactly that worker. add_comment
   gains `system=True` (no writer provenance); _tell_repair_card uses it.
3. The repair note says which case cleared the block ("every parent came
   back (parent_found)" vs "every parent link was removed ...
   (parents_unlinked); no parent came back").

RED on main (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_parent_missing_self_clear.py):
- test_every_parent_unlinked_...: source 'parent_found' != 'parents_unlinked'
- test_clearing_the_block_comments_on_the_open_repair_card: no "came back"
- test_the_repair_note_is_not_the_repair_workers_own_comment: payload had
  writer_run_id 1
GREEN with this change.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_db_comment_ids.py           | 12 ++++++--
 hermes_cli/kanban_db_graph.py                 | 28 +++++++++++--------
 .../test_kanban_parent_missing_self_clear.py  | 24 ++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

